---
import StateDiagram from "../components/StateDiagram.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { localUrl } from "../data/site";

const quickstart = [
  "orbitkv-cache-manager \\",
  "  --addr 127.0.0.1:50055 \\",
  "  --http-addr 127.0.0.1:9091 \\",
  "  --pool-size 8gb",
].join("\n");

const capabilities = [
  {
    title: "Reuse prefixes.",
    label: "DRAM + SSD",
    detail:
      "Keep useful KV beyond one request and restore it when a compatible prefix returns.",
    href: "/docs/single-node/",
  },
  {
    title: "Keep the Manager.",
    label: "Engine restart",
    detail:
      "Offload reusable KV to pinned DRAM and optional SSD. Keep the Manager alive across engine restarts.",
    href: "/docs/cache-policies/",
  },
  {
    title: "Match the state.",
    label: "Model identity",
    detail:
      "Start with dense Qwen3 configurations. Check historical evidence and current qualification limits before selecting a model.",
    href: "/docs/models/",
  },
];
---

<SiteLayout active="Overview">
  <section class="hero container" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">KV cache for vLLM and SGLang</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">
        Reuse KV.
        <br />
        Across
        <br />
        <span class="highlight">cache tiers.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="hero-description">
        Keep repeated documents, system prompts and conversation prefixes
        useful beyond GPU memory.{" "}
        <br />
        One Cache Manager per host. Your engine keeps control of execution.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button primary" href={localUrl("/docs/")}>
          Read the docs <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
        <a class="text-link" href="#get-started">
          Get started <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <StateDiagram />
  </section>
  <aside class="evidence-strip container" aria-label="Evidence and qualification status">
    <a href={localUrl("/docs/transport/")}>
      <span class="eyebrow">CI controls</span>
      <strong>CPU/TCP · io_uring</strong>
      <span>Byte and ownership controls; not hardware qualification. →</span>
    </a>
    <a href={localUrl("/docs/compatibility/")}>
      <span class="eyebrow">Unqualified</span>
      <strong>OrbiTE hardware paths</strong>
      <span>GPU, RDMA, GDS and installed profiles await hardware runs. →</span>
    </a>
    <a href={localUrl("/docs/performance/")}>
      <span class="eyebrow">Historical · TENT</span>
      <strong>Measurements with limits</strong>
      <span>Original revisions and verdicts; they do not qualify OrbiTE. →</span>
    </a>
  </aside>
  <section class="stack-section container" aria-labelledby="stack-title">
    <header class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">01 / Reuse</p>
        <h2 id="stack-title">
          Compute once.
          <br />
          Keep it useful.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <a class="text-link" href={localUrl("/architecture/")}>
        Explore the architecture <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </header>
    <div class="layer-grid">
      {capabilities.map((item) => (
        <article class="layer">
          <a class="package-name" href={localUrl(item.href)}>
            {item.label} <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
          <h3>{item.title}</h3>
          <p>{item.detail}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="provider-line">
      <span>Implemented</span> Engine-owned HBM · pinned DRAM · optional SSD{" "}
      <a href={localUrl("/docs/compatibility/")}>Hardware profiles unqualified →</a>
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="proof-band" aria-labelledby="evidence-title">
    <div class="container proof-inner">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">02 / Share</p>
        <h2 id="evidence-title">
          Start on one host.
          <br />
          Build toward a pool.
        </h2>
        <p>Local engines → shared Manager → compatible peer replicas</p>
      </div>
      <div class="proof-note">
        <p>
          OrbitKV owns cache identity, placement and source grants. OrbiTE moves
          bytes to the requested GPU or DRAM destination. Peer discovery uses
          local inventory indexes and leased membership; it does not authorize a read.
          Current peer GPU/RDMA and installed profiles remain unqualified.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href={localUrl("/docs/deployment/")}>
          Choose a deployment <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
        <a class="text-link" href={localUrl("/docs/pd/")}>
          Live P/D keeps the engine's native transport →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section
    class="get-started container"
    id="get-started"
    aria-labelledby="start-title"
  >
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">03 / Recover</p>
      <h2 id="start-title">
        Connect.
        <br />
        Run. Reuse.
      </h2>
      <p>
        Build an unreleased wheel, start a Manager, then enable your engine's
        adapter. Keep the Manager alive while restarting the engine to distinguish
        an external restore from a native GPU cache hit.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href={localUrl("/docs/single-node/#vllm")}>
        vLLM quickstart →
      </a>
      <br />
      <a class="text-link" href={localUrl("/docs/single-node/#sglang")}>
        SGLang quickstart →
      </a>
    </div>
    <figure class="code-panel">
      <div class="code-bar">Terminal / Cache Manager</div>
      <pre
        tabindex="0"
        aria-label="Start the Cache Manager"
      ><code>{quickstart}</code></pre>
      <figcaption class="code-notes">
        <p><strong>Before:</strong> complete the <a href={localUrl("/docs/single-node/")}>Linux/CUDA installation</a>. This is an unqualified hardware recipe.</p>
        <p><strong>Configure:</strong> <code>addr</code> selects the local socket seed; <code>pool-size</code> budgets host memory, not GPU memory. <a href={localUrl("/docs/server/")}>Option reference →</a></p>
        <p><strong>Verify:</strong> save a prompt, restart only the engine and require restored bytes to increase. <a href={localUrl("/docs/single-node/#check-behavior-and-capacity")}>Hit check →</a></p>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>
  <section class="stack-section container" aria-labelledby="learn-title">
    <header class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">04 / Documentation</p>
        <h2 id="learn-title">
          From first hit
          <br />
          to system design.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <a class="text-link" href={localUrl("/docs/")}>
        Browse all documentation →
      </a>
    </header>
    <div class="doc-links">
      <a href={localUrl("/docs/single-node/")}>
        Installation and engine setup <span>→</span>
      </a>
      <a href={localUrl("/architecture/")}>
        Architecture and ownership <span>→</span>
      </a>
      <a href={localUrl("/docs/metrics/")}>
        Metrics and operation <span>→</span>
      </a>
      <a href={localUrl("/docs/performance/")}>
        Benchmarks and measured limits <span>→</span>
      </a>
      <a href={localUrl("/docs/distributed-cache/")}>
        Distributed cache design <span>→</span>
      </a>
      <a href={localUrl("/docs/completion-plan/")}>
        Completion and validation gates <span>→</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
